@[boot-loader step]
Set up a boot loader, which starts the kernel when the machine boots. Each
choice has its own instructions:

  @[todo grub]      GRUB, on this ISO (the @[grub2] cache); BIOS and UEFI
  @[todo limine]    Limine: small and modern; BIOS and UEFI
  @[todo refind]    rEFInd: a boot menu; UEFI only
  @[todo syslinux]  SYSLINUX/EXTLINUX; BIOS only
  @[todo lilo]      LILO, the LInux LOader; BIOS only
  @[todo systemd-boot]  systemd-boot: with systemd (init-system step); UEFI

Only GRUB is on this ISO; the others need network (@[guide network]) to cast
them into the new system now, from @[enchantment chroot] (copy the live
system's DNS settings first: @[cp /etc/resolv.conf $ENCHANT_TARGET/etc/]). The new system needs a
working boot loader to start the first time, so GRUB is the simple choice;
you can switch later.

To see these instructions again, type @[todo]. When the boot loader is set
up, type @[next] to go on to the user setup.
